t the quantity  AR plus RC from the problem SR is equal  to RT is equal to 6 because each is a  radius of the circle  next what about the length of AC well AC  is a diagonal of this rectangle so it'll  be equal to the other diagonal which is  our B and our B is also a radius of the  circle therefore this is equal to 6  which means AC is also equal to 6  finally we have a R + RC  this is given to us in the problem as  the length plus width of the rectangle  which is equal to 8 so we now know each  of these quantities so we get 6 plus 6  plus 6 minus 8 and this simplifies to be  10 so we put these two parts together to  get that the perimeter of the shaded  region is equal to 10 plus 3 pi and  that's answer choice B did you figure it  out and what method did you use thanks  for watching this video please subscribe  to my channel I make videos on math you  can catch me on my blog mind your  decisions if you like this video you can  check out my books which are listed in  the video description and you can  support me on patreon you've got a math  topic or a suggestion you can email me  brush at mind your decisions calm and  you can reach me on social media either  at mind your decisions or at presh tell  walker
 

